WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.353
Scenario: A project teammate asks you to upload a

2
00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:06.706
spreadsheet containing student IDs and contact details to a

3
00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:10.059
folder with “Anyone with the link can view” access.

4
00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:13.412
Safest response: Option A: Share only with the verified

5
00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:16.765
people who need it, using an approved restricted channel

6
00:00:16.765 --> 00:00:20.118
and minimum necessary data. Verify recipients and classification, then

7
00:00:20.118 --> 00:00:23.471
apply least privilege to access and content. Option B

8
00:00:23.471 --> 00:00:26.824
is unsafe because Temporary broad exposure is still exposure;

9
00:00:26.824 --> 00:00:30.176
access should be appropriately restricted before sharing. Option C

10
00:00:30.176 --> 00:00:33.529
is unsafe because Renaming does not remove sensitive content

11
00:00:33.529 --> 00:00:36.882
or limit access. Option D is unsafe because A

12
00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:40.235
personal mailbox may bypass organizational controls and create a

13
00:00:40.235 --> 00:00:43.588
